 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+### Eviction Policy: 2Q
+
+Use a two-queue replacement policy to protect frequently accessed comparison sheets during large sequential screenings.
+
+**Queue A (new entries):** Entries admitted on first cache hit. Sized at 25% of the cache capacity (3 GiB). Entries evicted FIFO when A exceeds its bound, regardless of access after admission. Purpose: quickly shed one-use screening clips without preventing them from being rendered.
+
+**Queue B (reused entries):** Entries promoted to B on a second access while in the cache. Sized at 75% of the cache capacity (9 GiB). Entries in B are evicted LRU only after A is exhausted. Purpose: retain comparison-session clips across long screenings.
+
+**Promotion rule:** When a cached entry (in A or B) is accessed again, promote it to B if not already there. Record the access time for LRU ordering within B.
+
+**Eviction sequence:** When cache would exceed 12 GiB after admission:
+1. Evict the oldest FIFO entries from A until A is within its 3 GiB limit.
+2. If still over budget, evict the least recently used entries from B until under 12 GiB total.
+
+**Bookkeeping:** Maintain a lookup table keyed on preview key (clip ID + revision + renderer version) that stores: queue assignment (A or B), position/timestamp in queue, and entry size. On promotion or new admission, update the table; on access, check for promotion eligibility and update timestamp.
