 # Preview Specifications
 
+## Caching and Eviction
+
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-001**: When a request identifies an unknown clip revision, the system SHALL return 404 without enqueuing a render job.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-002**: When the requested preview is cached, the system SHALL return 200 with the JPEG for the requested revision and renderer version.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
-- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
-- [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## 2Q Eviction Policy
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When a preview is admitted to the cache for the first time, the system SHALL place it in Queue A.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: Queue A SHALL retain at most 3 GiB of cached JPEG data. When A exceeds this limit, the system SHALL evict the oldest entries (by admission time) until A is within bounds.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When a cached preview is accessed a second time while in Queue A, the system SHALL promote it to Queue B and record its access time.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: Queue B SHALL retain at most 9 GiB of cached JPEG data. When eviction is required and A is empty, the system SHALL evict entries from B using least-recently-used order until the total cache is within 12 GiB.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: When the cache would exceed 12 GiB after admitting a new preview, the system SHALL evict entries using the sequence: FIFO from A until A meets its bound, then LRU from B until total is within 12 GiB, then admit the new entry.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-015**: When a cached preview in Queue B is accessed, the system SHALL update its access timestamp without moving it.
